1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,845
Part 2 of local Oracle APEX for AI agents.

2
00:00:04,105 --> 00:00:10,216
In part 1, the agent ran APEX pages on a laptop, with SQLite instead of Oracle.

3
00:00:11,366 --> 00:00:14,232
But a real application lives in its database.

4
00:00:14,492 --> 00:00:18,902
Packages, triggers and real rows cannot be imitated in SQLite.

5
00:00:20,052 --> 00:00:23,394
So the local preview now connects to your own database.

6
00:00:23,654 --> 00:00:30,511
Add --env, and the Node.js backend opens one session to a DEV, QA or TEST schema,

7
00:00:30,771 --> 00:00:33,248
through your saved SQLcl connection.

8
00:00:34,398 --> 00:00:39,348
The UI still renders locally, with APEX's own templates and JavaScript.

9
00:00:39,608 --> 00:00:45,202
Region SQL runs in Oracle as written, with page items as binds.

10
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:50,656
Processes, validations and conditions run as real PL/SQL blocks.

11
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:57,264
With the app installed, a real APEX session makes v() and apex_util work.

12
00:00:58,414 --> 00:01:03,005
This stock-control app is connected to an Oracle Autonomous Database.

13
00:01:03,265 --> 00:01:06,274
Every figure and chart comes from the real tables.

14
00:01:07,424 --> 00:01:11,535
Post a draft receipt: the project's own package runs in Oracle.

15
00:01:11,795 --> 00:01:15,437
The page reports success, and the status is DRAFT again.

16
00:01:15,697 --> 00:01:18,508
The request was rolled back, so nothing was saved.

17
00:01:19,658 --> 00:01:21,137
Issue more than is on hand,

18
00:01:21,397 --> 00:01:24,643
and the package's own error appears as an APEX message.

19
00:01:25,793 --> 00:01:27,790
Every request ends with a rollback.

20
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:34,820
COMMIT and dynamic SQL in page code are never sent, and a tripwire catches commits from stored code.

21
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:38,968
Production is refused, and the database identity must match.

22
00:01:40,118 --> 00:01:45,881
All 17 pages checked against the real database: 21 seconds, 0 errors.

23
00:01:46,141 --> 00:01:48,933
A second session confirmed that no row was saved.

24
00:01:50,083 --> 00:01:52,103
Part 1: design on SQLite.

25
00:01:52,363 --> 00:01:55,109
Part 2: verify against the real logic.

26
00:01:55,369 --> 00:01:57,869
Then compile and import on a DEV target.

27
00:01:59,019 --> 00:02:01,860
Real database logic. Nothing persisted.

28
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:06,521
Rendering is still local: shipping still compiles and imports on DEV.

